{"entryId":"1126","paragraphs":[{"sourceId":"heilprin:sefaria-warsaw:ta:1126:1","sourceSha256":"355a9c5b20826f156cb415f0a6f9a3753454f9f4193a83160201e929c019ab86","englishSha256":"2674699445db43b72329d4883507141176f47e51c5816a2274de530405f9f20e","citations":[{"id":"1126:1:cite-01","he":[222,242],"en":[336,350],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_27b.19"},"reference":"Megillah 27b:19","assessment":"The student question, mother’s sale of her cap and the distinct counts of 300 and 3,000 are explicit. The narrative does not name the sons.","evidence":[{"reference":"Megillah 27b:19","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_27b.19"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Megillah 27b:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_27b.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"}]},{"id":"1126:1:cite-02","he":[298,309],"en":[421,436],"target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.24"},"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:24","assessment":"Two witnesses report 120 years for Rabban Yohanan ben Zakkai. Neither identifies the father as the longevity narrator in Megillah. Keep Heilprin's tentative proposal and immediate objection.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 357:33","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_357.33"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"}]}],"inlineHebrew":[0,1],"holds":[{"raw":"נראה שהוא אביו של ר' יוחנן","reason":"The longevity witnesses do not establish the proposed parentage. The compiler immediately raises a counterargument.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 357:33","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_357.33"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"}]},{"raw":"ועיין בסמוך מ\"ש שם","reason":"Nearby entry 1136 discusses Yochanan ben Zakkai, but no precise nearby passage matching the counter-parentage pointer was established.","evidence":[{"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 357:33","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_357.33"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"}]}],"notes":[{"text":"The student question, mother’s sale of her cap and the distinct counts of 300 and 3,000 are explicit. The narrative does not name the sons.","references":["Megillah 27b:19","Megillah 27b:20"],"urls":[]},{"text":"Two witnesses report 120 years for Rabban Yohanan ben Zakkai. Neither identifies the father as the longevity narrator in Megillah. Keep Heilprin's tentative proposal and immediate objection.","references":["Sanhedrin 41a:24","Sifrei Devarim 357:33"],"urls":[]},{"text":"The narrative has the mother sell her head covering; Rashi specifies a scarf. This supports an unforced translation of kippah as a head covering in this occurrence.","references":["Megillah 27b:19","Rashi on Megillah 27b:19:2"],"urls":[]}],"comparisonEvidence":[{"reference":"Megillah 27b:19","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_27b.19"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Megillah 27b:20","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Megillah_27b.20"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sanhedrin 41a:24","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sanhedrin_41a.24"},"witness":"William Davidson Edition - Vocalized Aramaic"},{"reference":"Sifrei Devarim 357:33","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Sifrei_Devarim_357.33"},"witness":"Sefaria Vocalized Edition"},{"reference":"Rashi on Megillah 27b:19:2","target":{"url":"https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Megillah_27b.19.2"},"witness":"Vilna Edition"}]}],"entryEvi